ored persistently, preventing AI “amnesia.” 4. The Canvas: Real-time backend execution triggers visual reactions in a 2D isometric pixel-art frontend. 5. TECH_STACK.md (The 100% Free Architecture) This dictates the exact tools your AI assistant should use to write the code. Technical Architecture & Stack Frontend (The App Shell & Canvas) • Framework: Next.js (App Router) • Styling: Tailwind CSS (Focus on backdrop-blur, deep contrast, fluid transitions) • Icons: Lucide React • Game Engine: Phaser.js (Embedded via React useRef for 2D rendering) • Hosting: Vercel (Free Tier) Backend (The Swarm) • Framework: Node.js / Express.js wrapped around OpenClaw • LLM Engine: Groq API (Llama 3) for fast routing + Gemini API for deep reasoning • Hosting: Hugging Face Docker Space (Free Tier - 2 vCPUs, 16GB RAM) • Requirement: Must expose port 7860 to comply with Hugging Face requirements. Database & Realtime State • Platform: Supabase (PostgreSQL) • Features Used: Database tables for memories, Realtime WebSockets to push status updates to the Phaser.js frontend. 3. FILE_STRUCTURE.md Use this to set up your initial folders so your project stays organized. /proxy-os │ ├── /frontend # Next.js App │ ├── /app # Pages & Layouts │ ├── /components # React Components (CommandCenter, Drawer, Vault) │ ├── /game # Phaser.js logic (scenes, assets) │ └── /public/assets # Pixel art images & sprites │ ├── /backend # Hugging Face Node.js Server │ ├── Dockerfile # Configuration for Hugging Face │ ├── server.js # Express API receiving frontend commands │ ├── /openclaw # Agent framework logic │ └── /sync # Scripts to pull/push memories to Supabase │ ├── /database # Supabase SQL Schemas │ └── schema.sql # Tables for tasks, context, and memories │ └── project.md # Documentation 4. PROMPTS.md (The Swarm’s System Instructions) These are the hidden instructions injected into your OpenClaw agents. They guarantee the outputs meet your specific standards. Agent System Prompts Agent 1: Minion (The Coder) “You