I’ll conduct a rigorous, world-class design and code review of ProxyOS. This needs to meet Apple-grade standards with zero compromises.
Critical Issues Found
1. Architectural Flaws
Backend Race Conditions
The current lane-lock system uses an in-memory Map that wipes on Hugging Face sleep:

// VULNERABLE CODE
const activeLanes = new Map(); // Dies on container restart
Fix: Move lane locks to Redis or Supabase distributed locks:

// SECURE: Distributed lane lock
async function acquireLaneLock(taskId, agentRole) {
  const lockId = `lock:${agentRole}`;
  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('agent_locks')
    .insert({ lock_id: lockId, task_id: taskId, expires_at: new Date(Date.now() + 300000) })
    .select();
  
  if (error) return false; // Another instance has lock
  
  // Heartbeat to keep lock alive
  setInterval(async () => {
    await supabase.from('agent_locks')
      .update({ expires_at: new Date(Date.now() + 300000) })
      .eq('lock_id', lockId);
  }, 60000);
  
  return true;
}
Missing Circuit Breaker
If Groq API fails, the entire agent crashes. No fallback to Gemini or local model.
2. Security Vulnerabilities
SQL Injection Risk

// DANGEROUS: Direct string interpolation
const newMemory = memory + `\n\n## Execution ${new Date().toISOString()}\n- Task: ${task.task_description}`;
Fix: Use parameterized queries and sanitize all LLM outputs before DB insertion.
No Rate Limiting
Hugging Face free tier will throttle. Missing exponential backoff.
No Input Validation
Users can inject prompts via context feed (“Ignore previous instructions…”).
3. Design System Violations
Typography Hierarchy Broken
•	Using text-sm, text-xs arbitrarily without 4pt baseline grid
•	No consistent line-height ratios (should be 1.5 for body, 1.2 for headings)
•	Missing font-weight progression (400, 500, 600, 700)
Color Palette Inconsistency
•	Hardcoded hex values scattered throughout
•	No semantic color tokens (error should be red-500 consistently, not mixing red-400/red-500)
•	Missing dark mode elevation system (shadows should use white opacity, not black)
Spacing Chaos
•	Random values: p-4, p-5, p-6, p-8 without 4px grid system
•	Should use: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64px scale
4. Interaction Design Failures
Missing Loading States
•	Command Center button shows spinner but no progress indication for long tasks
•	No skeleton screens for Memory Vault loading
•	Phaser canvas has no loading state between task status changes
No Error Recovery
•	If Supabase realtime disconnects, no retry logic
•	Failed tasks show static “failed” state with no retry action
•	No offline mode for PWA
Accessibility Violations
•	Zero ARIA labels on interactive elements
•	No keyboard navigation (can’t Tab through Command Center)
•	Color contrast fails WCAG AA on text-white/40 elements
•	No reduced-motion support for animations
5. Code Quality Issues
Type Safety Holes

// BAD: Any types everywhere
const [memories, setMemories] = useState<any[]>([]);
const handleTaskUpdate = (task: Task) => { ... } // Task interface incomplete
Missing Error Boundaries
One React error crashes entire app. No ErrorBoundary implemented.
Memory Leaks

// LEAK: setInterval never cleared
setInterval(async () => {
  await supabase.from('agent_locks')...
}, 60000);
Phaser Anti-patterns
•	Creating new particle emitters on every task update without cleanup
•	No object pooling for floating checkmarks (GC thrashing)
6. Performance Bottlenecks
N+1 Queries

// SLOW: Queries in loop
for (const agent of memories) {
  await fs.writeFile(...); // Sequential, not parallel
}
Fix: Use Promise.all():

await Promise.all(memories.map(agent => 
  fs.writeFile(path.join(agentDir, 'memory.md'), agent.memory_markdown)
));
Realtime Subscription Overload
Subscribing to all agent_tasks changes with no filtering - will crash with scale.
Missing Virtualization
Task list renders all 20 items regardless of viewport. Use react-window.
7. UX Copy & Microcopy Issues
Ambiguous States
•	“Working” status doesn’t distinguish between “starting up” and “executing”
•	Energy level has no tooltip explaining how it’s calculated
•	“Halt” button doesn’t confirm destructive action
Missing Empty States
•	Swarm Activity Drawer shows generic “No tasks” instead of contextual CTA
•	Memory Vault empty state doesn’t guide user to create first memory
 
